{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And I will take a morsel of bread</b> — it should have said, \"take a morsel of bread.\" This hints that the host breaks the bread himself." "<b>לבכם</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: שיתו לבכם לחילה, and וראיתם ושש לבכם. And this is what they said: that he was distressed that no guests had come to him — and this is שיתו לבכם, that he was distressed in his heart when he saw these; and שש לבכם."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:19.851499670Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}